1. What this notice covers

This notice covers the original work in this repository and any website built
from it (ap.matty.se): the source code, the explanatory texts and their
translations, the figures and design, and the selection, arrangement and
annotation of the data (including the source and verification records in
assets/data/properties.json). Individual facts and values reported in the
literature or in public sources are not claimed; third-party material is
listed in section 4.

2. What you may do

- View the website and the source code.
- Clone or download the repository for private study, teaching and evaluation
  (for example by reviewers or editors).
- Link to the website or the repository and cite the work.
- Fork the repository on GitHub, as permitted by GitHub's Terms of Service.

3. What requires prior written permission

You may not copy, modify, distribute, publish, host, sublicense or sell this
work or any part of it, or create derivative works from it, beyond what
section 2 allows, without prior written permission from the copyright holder.

4. Third-party material (excluded; remains under its own terms)

- Receptor-binding data from the IUPHAR/BPS Guide to Pharmacology (database
  ODbL, contents CC BY-SA 4.0) and ChEMBL (CC BY-SA 3.0).
- Molecular weights from PubChem (NCBI; public domain).
- Values from FDA prescribing information (DailyMed, openFDA) and from the EU
  summaries of product characteristics published in FASS (texts copyright of
  the marketing-authorization holders and Läkemedelsindustriföreningen; only
  facts and short quotations are used, with citation).
- Values from the published literature, each cited in assets/data/properties.json.
- Model data listed in assets/models/NOTICE (PDB entries 6CM4, 6LUQ and 8U02,
  CC0; FreeSurfer fsaverage and the ICBM 152 2009c template via TemplateFlow) and
  the structure drawings described in assets/images/structures/NOTICE.
- JavaScript libraries loaded from CDNs (Plotly.js, 3Dmol.js, three.js, KaTeX)
  and the Inter font, under their own licenses.

Sources and their licenses are listed in assets/data/properties.json
(references) and on the data page (properties.html).

